# Quality Gates

All changes must pass these quality gates before marking a story as complete.

## Required Checks

| Gate | Requirement | Command (typical) |
|------|-------------|-------------------|
| **Build** | Compiles without errors | `npm run build` |
| **Typecheck** | No type errors | `npm run typecheck` or `tsc --noEmit` |
| **Lint** | No linting errors | `npm run lint` |
| **Tests** | All tests pass | `npm test` |

### Build Verification

After completing any task, verify:
- The project builds without errors
- All existing tests pass
- No new linter errors introduced

Use the appropriate build commands for your project type (npm, pnpm, dotnet, cargo, etc.).

> ⚠️ **Do NOT rely on IDE linter alone** - always verify with CLI before completing a story.

## Definition of Done

A story is complete when:

- [ ] All acceptance criteria met
- [ ] Build passes without errors or warnings
- [ ] Type checking passes
- [ ] Linting passes
- [ ] Existing tests still pass
- [ ] New tests added for non-trivial logic
- [ ] No secrets or credentials in code
- [ ] Changes committed with clear message
- [ ] PRD updated with `passes: true`
- [ ] Progress log updated

## UI/Frontend Stories

Additional requirements for stories that change user interface:

- [ ] **Production build passes** (run your project's build command)
- [ ] Verified in browser (not just build passing)
- [ ] Works on target viewport sizes
- [ ] No console errors
- [ ] Accessible (keyboard navigation, screen reader)

## Code Quality Standards

### DO

- Follow existing patterns in the codebase
- Handle errors appropriately
- Add meaningful comments for complex logic
- Use descriptive variable and function names
- Keep functions focused and small

### DON'T

- Commit broken code
- Skip tests for "simple" changes
- Leave TODO comments for critical issues
- Disable linting rules without justification
- Hardcode configuration values

## Commit Message Format

Use the canonical commit-type table in the main prompt (`feat:`, `fix:`, `refactor:`, `test:`, `docs:`, `chore:`). Format: `<type>: (<jira-id>) description` or `<type>: <story-id> - description`.

## Failure Recovery

If a quality gate fails:

1. **Identify** - Which check failed and why
2. **Fix** - Address the issue directly
3. **Re-verify** - Run all checks again
4. **Document** - Note any gotchas in progress.txt

Do NOT bypass quality gates. If genuinely blocked, document in progress.txt and end the iteration.
